1. REPORT ON PAST RESEARCH (OPTIONAL)

I graduated with distinction (program topper) from Symbiosis International University with a
MTech (Master of Technology) degree in Geoinformatics & Surveying Technology. I successfully
completed my master thesis under the TREES (Training and Research in Earth Eco-System)
program organized by Space Application Center (SAC), Indian Space Research Organization
(ISRO), under the supervision of Dr. Gaurav Jain. My thesis was focused on determining optimal
solar power plant locations for supplementing electrical vehicle charging using remote sensing
inputs and environmental parameters. We identified a network of EV charging stations that met
the governmental regulations, and we developed a balancing algorithm to better estimate the area
of solar panels needed to supply energy demands while optimizing the use of barren/empty lands
in the vicinity. The final output of this research methodology was the ability to develop a map
containing the suitable optimized charging network that incorporates the placement solar panels
in identified barren lands, while considering the optimization of solar radiant energy received by
surfaces through Global Horizontal Irradiance (GHI) parameter. This GHI data was confidential
and was made available due to special nature of TREES internship, making this research truly
unique within the organization only, and making an important new addition to the state of art.

In my final year, I was hired as a Junior Research Fellow in Department of Science & Technology
(DST) & IC-IMPACT’s Indo Canada Building Energy Optimization under landscape characteristics
project, which involved the use of a LoRa sensor network for hyperlocal sensing of thermal
comfort across different land surfaces in different configurations. Working in this project gave me
opportunity to use LoRaWAN technology to setup in-situ sensors that collected data for modeling
urban thermal comfort, which shares similarities and demonstrated my expertise for the present
doctoral project. After acquiring the hyperlocal data, satellite-based observations were used for
ground validation of Building Energy models. Additionally, I was exposed to work with the
integrating IoT sensors on Amazon Web Services (AWS). In this project we submitted a paper in
Urban Climate Journal (Q1) which is under review, and presented a paper in Flame Conference
on Climate Change which was held in Dec 2021, that will be published in conference proceedings
in 2022.

In my senior year, my team won Global Nasa Space Apps Challenge due to our crowdsource
data fusion application for critical disaster assessment, which is currently under communication
with the WALMI center in Gujarat, India. This project involved the use of crowdsourced data from
volunteers in flood regions, where they can take pictures using an app that applied an auto geotag
to photos and added them to the SQL Database, which we could retrieve and apply a time-space
comparison allowing visualization over pre and post-flood scenarios. Authorities could use this
app to get a live visualization of pre & post-flood scenarios, and reduce disaster rescue action
delays due to lack of information. This project involved the use of near real-time data under cloud-
free and image quality filters.

My undergrad final year project received an AICTE fund of ₹1.67 million and facilitated purchasing
Ideaforge’s Ninja Nano UAV with Night Vision surveillance, live human tracking, and time-based
crime surveillance. This project was my final year thesis in B. Tech work on Smart Crime
Management in Smart Cities, which used past data scrapping from news articles and geocoding
their locations in space and time to understand crime patterns, predict crime possibilities, evaluate
crime vulnerability, and subsidize those vulnerabilities by adding patrolling routes and placing
more police stations and patrol vehicles in such neighborhoods.

In 2021 during my final year of M. Tech, we received approval from AICTE and got the Ideaforge’s
Ninja Nano UAV with 3 payloads (thermal Infrared, Photogrammetry and TCC video imagery)
delivered to the Birla Vishwakarma Mahavidyalaya (B. Tech) university, and a personal was
authorized to conduct training for the drone flight by manufacturer. I received that training in
December 2021, and each member of my team got a chance to perform VTOL, orientation and
create mission plan in Ideaforge’s software, and to independently deploy drones.

