In December 2019, I presented two papers in Symbiosis National Conference SYMGI-2019.
During this time I met with Prof. Sharvari Shukla who is the director of Symbiosis Statistical
Institute (SSI), and she gave me an opportunity to contribute a Springer Book Chapter, on
Geointelligence. During the Covid19 crisis, the use of Public Health, Mass Safety and Geography
became important, demanding an intelligence hub containing information from land features and
geophysical properties to human altercations, mobility, and resource utilization. In the Covid19
crisis, I got involved in drafting paper on the application of Geointelligence for healthcare,
especially in a developing country such as India. This book is published this year in 2022.

While working on this springer book chapter, I got the change to collaborate with Prof. Prasad
Pathak, who is Research Dean at Flame University. He had received the DST-ICIMPACT grant
for Indo-Canada Building Energy Optimization project, and he allowed me to begin working in this
project as a Junior Research Fellow, during my final year of M. Tech since April 2021. Within the
bounds of JRF at Flame University, I also got the opportunity to order experimental sensors and
camera lens such as fish eye lenses and a thermal imager, which were designed for gathering
spectral imagery across inter-building distances to analyze the radial extent to which a surface
warms its neighborhood within Urban Heat Island Effect. The use of a fish eye lens facilitated
gathering 130-degree images which were useful in gathering Sky View Factor (SVF) values by
orienting the camera towards Zenith and taking pictures of sky, and later digitizing the surrounding
features that would limit sky view. This was also useful in linking the inbound solar radiation
(Global Horizontal Irradiance) values towards the open to sky surface areas that receive solar
energy for major part of day, especially when the sun is at maximum inclination. This research
explored the understanding of radiation interactivity and cross-heating which warmed the air
temperature registered in LoRa sensors across different surface nature & configurations.

In 2021, towards my final year of M. Tech I participated with a team of students in Mapathon
competition organized by Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay, for which my team became the
Mapathon Champion by competing again 9300 entries, where we had designed an Electrical
Vehicle Charging Network Plan based on excess surplus energy generated at power stations,
residential energy usage, and the proximity of nearby charging infrastructure using Resourcesat
Satellite’s LISS-III data and the algorithm of Maximum Likelihood Classifier. Petrol Stations within
the range of Power Lines (to avoid transmission loss) were identified for the Electrical Vehicle
Charging Network, and the areas selected where those areas requested by the Ministry of Power
(2018) (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ubGp76LAhmE).

In final semester of my M. Tech, I won Varanasi Smart Hackathon. With this event government
of Varanasi was planning to get Smart City status and they were inviting students with tech ideas
for innovation to build smart solutions for many industrial problems such as transportation,
pollution, etc. My team’s idea was to subsidize renewable energy and use electric mobility
technology. The network planning was done using satellite data and spatial city attributes taken
from Open Streets Map. Existing electric infrastructure with the existing residential mapping was
done for identifying the supportive locations where charging station can be established. This idea
facilitated us in winning 1st place and a reward of iPad Air. The government is presently deciding
their funding priorities, but they requested us to assist them in developing EV Infrastructure using
our optimization solution.

I have been interested in immersive reality since 2016, when VR technology became accessible
to public, with YouTube launching the first 360 immersive videos and with the release of the app
VR box. I received a student license for the VR Max software by Autodesk and Open-Source
software called Blender in order to learn how 3D movies can be made for VR. Further, I did
Certified Training Courses on Campus during my undergrad on Quantum GIS (QGIS), IDRISI,
DGPS (Differential GPS), AutoCAD, and 3D Laser Scanning. I also enrolled in Personality
Development Program (PDP) organized by Globarena Pvt. Ltd. In 2017.

